{
    "background_story": "Mohammed was a brilliant and eccentric scientist who spent most of his life studying the properties of energy. He became obsessed with the concept of exhaustibility, pouring over theories and conducting experiments to prove that even the most seemingly limitless resources could be depleted. His colleagues often joked that Mohammed's own energy was exhaustible, as he would work for days on end without rest, fueled by his passion for discovery. Despite his tireless efforts, Mohammed's health began to suffer, and he was forced to take breaks to recharge. However, even in his downtime, his mind continued to whir with ideas, and he would often scribble notes in the middle of the night. Mohammed's groundbreaking research eventually led to a major breakthrough in sustainable energy, but not before he had pushed his own body and mind to the limits of human endurance.",
